IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fraud-nouns`

-- Fraud Act 2006 (2006 c. 35), section 15: COMMENCEMENT AND EXTENT.
--
-- What is encoded: when the Act is in force (section 15(1)), where it extends (section 15(2) and
-- (3)).  Section 15(4) concerns where amendments made by section 10 and Schedule 1 extend; it
-- depends on the extent of the Acts amended, which are not among the sources, so it is not
-- encoded (see the coverage table in NOTES.md).
--
-- Commencement is left to an order, so the day appointed is an input, never a figure.
-- Extent is a different thing from application: it says where the Act is part of the law, and it
-- says nothing about conduct abroad or in Scotland that a court in England and Wales or
-- Northern Ireland could try; the Act does not answer that.

§ `Section 15: commencement and extent`

§§ `Section 15(1): commencement by order`

-- src:139 | 15 Commencement and extent
-- src:140 | (1) This Act (except this section and section 16) comes into force on such day as the Secretary of State may appoint by an order made by statutory instrument; and different days may be appointed for different purposes.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 15(1) (src:140)
GIVEN `the day appointed by order for the purpose` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 15(1): the Act is in force for a purpose on` `the day appointed by order for the purpose` `the day in question` MEANS
    -- NOTHING means that no day has been appointed for that purpose: until one is, the Act
    -- (except sections 15 and 16) is not in force for it.
    CONSIDER `the day appointed by order for the purpose`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST appointed THEN `the day in question` AT LEAST appointed

§§ `Section 15(2) and (3): extent`

-- src:141 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), sections 1 to 9 and 11 to 13 extend to England and Wales and Northern Ireland only.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 15(2) (src:141)
GIVEN place IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 15(2): sections 1 to 9 and 11 to 13 extend to` place MEANS
        place EQUALS `England`
    OR  place EQUALS `Wales`
    OR  place EQUALS `Northern Ireland`

-- src:142 | (3) Section 8, so far as it relates to the Armed Forces Act 2001 (c. 19), extends to any place to which that Act extends.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 15(3) (src:142)
GIVEN `the Armed Forces Act 2001 extends to the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 15(3): section 8, so far as it relates to the Armed Forces Act 2001, extends to the place` `the Armed Forces Act 2001 extends to the place` MEANS
    -- Borrowed term: where the Armed Forces Act 2001 extends is not in the sources, so it is a fact.
    `the Armed Forces Act 2001 extends to the place`
